            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Punjabi for a hair tassel, then the Punjabi for a lock of hair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ਸਜਾਉਣਾ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਸਜਾਉਣਾ — sajāuṇā — \"to arrange neatly; to decorate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਮੈਂ ਅਲਮਾਰੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਕਿਤਾਬਾਂ ਸਜਾਉਂਦੀ ਹਾਂ। maiṁ almārī vich kitābāṁ sajāundī hāṁ. I arrange the books neatly in the cupboard."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ਮੈਂ ਕਿਤਾਬਾਂ ਸਜਾਈਆਂ, maiṁ kitābāṁ sajāīāṁ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਸਜਾਉਣਾ (sajāuṇā) is inherited from Sanskrit sajjayati, \"equips, prepares\"; CDIAL lists Punjabi sajāuṇā, \"to prepare\" and Lahnda sajāvaṇ, \"to adorn\" (CDIAL 13091), but does not give the sense \"arrange neatly\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what you do."
            }
          ]
        },
